MCQ Question Paper

Q1. Who developed the Java programming language?
A. Microsoft B. Sun Microsystems C. Apple D. Google

Q2. Easy: What is the full form of E-Commerce?
A. Electrical Commerce B. Electronic Commerce C. Engineering Commerce D. Entertainment Commerce

Q3. An array in Java is a collection of which type of elements?
A. Heterogeneous B. Homogeneous C. Random D. Dynamic

Q4. In the statement 'Room r1 = new Room();', what specific task does the 'new' keyword perform?
A. It declares the variable r1. B. It initializes the object's variables. C. It allocates memory for the object on the heap. D. It destroys the previous object.

Q5. Java is a ______ programming language.
A. Procedural B. Functional C. Object-oriented D. Assembly

Q6. What is the full form of 'GSWAN'?
A. Gujarat State Wide Area Network B. Global Software Area Network C. General System Wide Area Network D. Gujarat Software Access Network

Q7. What is the primary purpose of an HTML form on a web page?
A. To play video files B. To collect user input and send it to a server C. To format the layout of the page D. To display static images

Q8. In the Object-Oriented paradigm, what is the focus compared to procedural programming?
A. Functions only B. Data and functionality together C. Procedures and modules D. Global variables

Q9. Easy: What is the first step in planning a website?
A. Deciding the Purpose B. Writing the Code C. Creating the Graphics D. Hosting the Website

Q10. Easy: What does M-Commerce stand for?
A. Modern Commerce B. Machine Commerce C. Mobile Commerce D. Multi-media Commerce

Q11. What does CSS stand for in web development?
A. Computer Style Sheets B. Creative Style System C. Cascading Style Sheets D. Colorful Style Sheets

Q12. What is the machine language for the Java Virtual Machine (JVM) called?
A. Source code B. Native code C. Java bytecode D. Assembly

Q13. Medium: Which website is cited as a prime example of an online bookstore in the text?
A. www.ebay.com B. www.amazon.com C. www.facebook.com D. www.google.com

Q14. A 1-D data structure is often referred to as a:
A. Matrix B. Vector C. Table D. Grid

Q15. What is the specific compilation error or result if a static method tries to access an instance variable directly?
A. It compiles but throws a runtime error. B. It creates a new instance automatically. C. It causes a compilation error because instance variables belong to objects. D. It treats the instance variable as a local variable.

Q16. A class in Java contains:
A. Only data B. Only methods C. Data and methods D. Only constructors

Q17. What does 'WYSIWYG' stand for?
A. What You See Is What You Get B. Where You See Is Where You Go C. Why You See Is What You Get D. What You Saw Is What You Got

Q18. Which attribute of the `<form>` tag specifies the HTTP method used to send data?
A. action B. name C. method D. type

Q19. Which term describes a template for multiple objects with similar features?
A. Attribute B. Method C. Class D. Instance

Q20. Medium: In the Table Properties dialog box in KompoZer, what does 'Spacing' control?
A. The space between the table and the text B. The space between cells C. The space between content and cell borders D. The width of the table

